Patchy patch for the macOS Qt 6.8.3 cocoa platform plugin (libqcocoa.dylib).

QTBUG-134784: a placeholder table cell element is put into QAccessibleCache
without a reference, but -invalidate releases one when the cell's interface is
deleted. A model reset (QListWidget::clear, which every Layers panel refresh
does) then frees cells a row's columns array still holds, and releasing the row
crashes in -[QMacAccessibilityElement dealloc] (GitHub issue 95). The upstream
fix (qtbase 0ee6ee5) is in Qt 6.8.4, which is commercial-only, and it also
changes QtGui; this patch fixes the reference count in the plugin alone.
Applied by scripts/setup-qt-cocoa-patch-mac.sh. Drop it at the next Qt bump
(docs/building.md, "Patched Qt cocoa plugin").

Qt is licensed under LGPL-3.0 (among other options); this file is the complete
source change to the shipped libqcocoa.dylib.

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoaaccessibilityelement.mm b/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoaaccessibilityelement.mm
index a07c9fe..93c0efe 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoaaccessibilityelement.mm
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/cocoa/qcocoaaccessibilityelement.mm
@@ -355,7 +355,8 @@ static void convertLineOffset(QAccessibleTextInterface *text, int *line, int *of
         synthesizedRole = nil;
 
         QAccessibleCache *cache = QAccessibleCache::instance();
-        if (QMacAccessibilityElement *cellElement = cache->elementForId(axid)) {
+        QMacAccessibilityElement *cellElement = cache->elementForId(axid);
+        if (cellElement) {
             // there already is another, non-placeholder element in the cache
             Q_ASSERT(cellElement->synthesizedRole == nil);
             // we have to release it if it's not us
@@ -365,7 +366,18 @@ static void convertLineOffset(QAccessibleTextInterface *text, int *line, int *of
             }
         }
 
-        cache->insertElement(axid, self);
+        // Patchy (QTBUG-134784): the cache owns one reference to each element it holds,
+        // which -invalidate releases when the cell interface is deleted (a model reset
+        // deletes them all). A placeholder is owned only by its row's columns array, so
+        // the cache takes its own reference here; without it, deleting the cell interface
+        // frees a cell the array still holds, and releasing the row later crashes. An
+        // element the cache already holds for this cell gives its reference up first.
+        if (cellElement != self) {
+            if (cellElement)
+                [cellElement invalidate];
+            cache->insertElement(axid, self);
+            [self retain];
+        }
     }
     return iface;
 }
